L168: baby-f: A filtered version of baby-base with all direct positive evidence sentences for the four target phenomena (cite107†Table 1 ) removed, simulating a learner exposed only to indirect evidence. Filtering details and sanity check in cite48†Appendix C .
L169: baby: Created from baby-f by replacing a small proportion of sentences with direct positive evidence examples ($\approx$0.2% for question formation; $\approx$0.07% for binding), maintaining identical sentence count while reintroducing the sparse direct evidence characteristic of children’s natural input. We construct both baby-f and baby only for 10–50M scales, as the 100M condition exceeds developmentally plausible early acquisition, where the PoS argument is most relevant.
